{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Function.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Function.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"azure function azure function","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Function.md","fileName":"Azure Function.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Azure Function","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Azure Logic Apps and Functions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Logic Apps and Functions","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Function.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Function.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"azure function azure function","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Azure Function.md","fileName":"Azure Function.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Azure Function","heading":"Azure Function","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An Azure Function is a small stateless unit of code invoked by a configured trigger and hosted with managed scaling. The developer supplies the operation while Azure supplies and scales the execution infrastructure, which is why the model is described as serverless.\n\nThe book's C# function compares dates for a logic app and returns a compact result. A function is useful when a high-level workflow reaches a calculation that is clearer or more reliable in ordinary code.\n\nThe book frames an Azure Function as a small event-triggered unit hosted under a Function App, with execution and scaling governed by the selected plan and bindings connecting inputs and outputs to Azure services.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Logic Apps and Functions","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEn